invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: an AES=runtime QUIC object hands the whole blocks of a schedule
  the table runs to the AES instructions, so a session whose caller's
  probe found no AES instructions executes them on every Initial packet
  and dies of SIGILL on the CPU that probe described. Both ciphers compute
  the same bytes, so no vector notices. aes_encrypt_counter_blocks
  asserts that its schedule runs on the instructions, and
  bin/aes_runtime_test seals and opens RFC 9001's Initial packets under
  the absent answer, so the assertion stops that binary.

--- old
    if (!on_instructions(k)) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    if (k == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }
